{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "patient-care",
    "title": "Patient Care",
    "order": 4
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "patient-identifiers",
    "title": "Patient ID & Safety Protocols",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The RTT's Prime Directive - Patient Safety",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Purpose: Why This Matters This lesson instills a thorough understanding of critical patient identification protocols, treatment site verification procedures, and overarching safety measures essential in the radiation therapy environment to prevent errors and ensure patient well-being."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Task: What You Will Do Learn about standardized identification methods, techniques for site verification, common safety checks, and the RTT's vital role in maintaining a safe treatment environment."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Criteria for Success Understand and be able to describe multi-step patient ID processes, methods for treatment site verification, and key daily safety protocols."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Patient safety is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "paramount",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " in radiation therapy. National Patient Safety Goals (NPSGs), such as those established by The Joint Commission, emphasize key areas like \"Identify patients correctly\" and \"Improve staff communication,\" which are directly relevant to our daily practice. As an RTT, you are a crucial guardian of patient safety."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Correct Patient Identification - The \"Two Identifier\" Rule & Beyond",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Accurate patient identification is the first and one of the most critical steps to prevent wrong-patient medical errors."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Standard Protocol: Using At Least Two Identifiers"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Always use "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "at least two unique patient identifiers",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " before initiating any procedure or treatment. Examples include:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Patient's full name"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Date of birth (DOB)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Medical Record Number (MRN) or other assigned unique ID number"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Patient photograph (cross-referenced with other identifiers)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Active Patient Involvement:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Actively involve the patient in the identification process. Ask them to "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "state their full name and date of birth",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Avoid leading questions such as, \"Are you John Smith?\" or \"Is your birthday January 1st?\""
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Verification Sources:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Cross-reference the patient's stated identifiers with information on the treatment chart, Electronic Medical Record (EMR), consent forms, and any physical identifiers (e.g., inpatient wristband)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Unacceptable identifiers for primary confirmation include the patient's room number or a verbal confirmation from another staff member who hasn't just actively verified the patient themselves."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "q_page2_1_ans",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Quick Check: Which is the BEST method to confirm a patient's identity before starting a procedure?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Checking the name on the door of the waiting room cubicle.",
              "Asking the patient to state their full name and date of birth, then matching it to the chart.",
              "Asking \"Are you Mrs. Johnson?\""
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": null
          },
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Check Answer"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Treatment Site & Laterality Verification",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Verifying the correct treatment site, including side (laterality, e.g., left vs. right), is essential before every fraction."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Multi-Point Verification Sources:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Radiation Oncologist\u2019s signed prescription and detailed treatment plan."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Simulation images, setup instructions, diagrams, and photographs."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Patient\u2019s skin markings/tattoos and their relation to the planned isocenter."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Immobilization devices and their indexed setup positions."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Treatment console parameters matching the approved plan for the correct site and laterality."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The \"Time Out\" Procedure:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A mandatory, active pause taken by the treatment team (typically two RTTs) "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "immediately before initiating the beam",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". During the Time Out, the team verbally confirms:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Correct patient (using two identifiers)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Correct treatment site and laterality (e.g., \"Left Breast\")."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Correct treatment plan loaded and parameters (e.g., gantry, collimator, couch angles, MUs) matched."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Correct accessories (bolus, wedges, etc.) and their orientation, if applicable."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Agreement between all team members present."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When in doubt, STOP and verify.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Any mismatch or uncertainty must be resolved before proceeding, involving dosimetry, physics, or the oncologist if necessary."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "q_page3_1_ans",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Quick Check: A \"Time Out\" procedure is performed:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Only for the first treatment fraction.",
              "After the treatment is completed to document settings.",
              "Immediately before initiating the beam for each treatment."
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": null
          },
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Check Answer"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Daily Safety Checks & Creating a Safe Environment",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "RTTs are responsible for ensuring the safety of the equipment and the treatment environment daily."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Linac & Equipment Safety:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Perform daily machine warm-up and Quality Assurance (QA) checks per institutional protocol. This often includes checking: "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Safety interlocks (e.g., door, beam-on indicators)."
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Audio and visual patient monitoring systems."
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Emergency stop buttons functionality."
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Laser alignment and ODI/rangefinder accuracy."
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " "
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Report any equipment malfunctions or QA deviations immediately to medical physics or engineering."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Treatment Room Environment & Patient Safety:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Ensure the room is clear of obstacles and unnecessary items."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Verify correct treatment accessories (wedges, electron cones, bolus) are selected, in good condition, and correctly oriented."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Confirm patient monitoring systems are functional."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Ensure the patient is secure and as comfortable as possible in immobilization devices."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Provide clear instructions to the patient to remain still and how to communicate if needed."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Maintain continuous audio and visual contact during beam-on."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Responding to Emergencies & Unexpected Events",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Being prepared for the unexpected is crucial."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Medical Emergencies:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Recognize signs of patient distress (difficulty breathing, chest pain, altered mental status, seizure, etc.)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Know how to activate your facility's emergency response system (e.g., \"Code Blue,\" rapid response)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Be prepared to initiate Basic Life Support (BLS) as per your training."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Equipment Malfunctions:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Know the location and operation of all emergency stop buttons on the Linac and couch."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Understand procedures for safely assisting the patient off the couch if the machine stops unexpectedly."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Report all malfunctions immediately according to facility protocol."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Other Emergencies & Incident Reporting:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Be familiar with fire safety procedures (RACE: Rescue, Alarm, Contain, Extinguish/Evacuate)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Understand your facility's specific codes for other emergencies."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Incident Reporting:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Report all incidents, errors (even those that don't reach the patient), and \"near misses.\" This is vital for a culture of safety and continuous quality improvement."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "q_page5_1_ans",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Quick Check: If you make an error that does NOT reach the patient (a \"near miss\"), should you still report it?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "No, because no harm was done.",
              "Yes, to help prevent future errors and improve systems.",
              "Only if your supervisor sees it happen."
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": null
          },
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Check Answer"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary & Activity Link",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Patient safety is the absolute priority in radiation therapy. This lesson highlighted:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "The non-negotiable importance of "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "accurate patient identification",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " using at least two active identifiers."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Critical need for meticulous "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "treatment site and laterality verification",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " at multiple checkpoints."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
